From: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 08 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: fix page_pool double-release on LRO error path

In airoha_qdma_rx_process(), when an LRO aggregate fails parsing
(airoha_qdma_lro_rx_process() returns < 0 for non-TCP, or pskb_may_pull
failure on the L2/L3/L4 headers), control jumps to free_frag: before
skb_mark_for_recycle() has been called on q->skb.

The free_frag: path then does:

	dev_kfree_skb(q->skb);              /* frees head as if kmalloc'd */
	page_pool_put_full_page(q->page_pool, page, true);

q->skb was built around the same page via napi_build_skb() and that
page is also referenced by the local `page` variable, so it is
released twice:

  1. dev_kfree_skb() -> skb_free_head() -> kfree(head) on a page_pool
     page (pp_recycle bit not set, since skb_mark_for_recycle() was
     deferred to the success path).
  2. page_pool_put_full_page() then decrements pp_ref_count again.

The second decrement underflows pp_ref_count, tripping
WARN_ON(ret < 0) in page_pool_unref_netmem() (helpers.h:297) and
leaves the page_pool / slab in a corrupted state. Observed on a
W1700K (AN7581) acting as a router with LRO enabled on wan: two
back-to-back warnings ~8.5 h into uptime, followed by silent RX
death on an unrelated interface ~11 h later.

Fix by marking the skb for recycle immediately after napi_build_skb()
so that any subsequent error path within the first-buffer branch
releases the page exactly once via dev_kfree_skb(). Replace the
goto free_frag in the LRO error path with an explicit
dev_kfree_skb()+continue so we do not also call page_pool_put_full_page()
on the same page.

Fixes: 916-net-airoha-Implement-LRO-TCP-support (out-of-tree)
Signed-off-by: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -834,14 +834,17 @@ static int airoha_qdma_rx_process(struct
 			skb_reserve(q->skb, AIROHA_RX_HEADROOM);
 			__skb_put(q->skb, len);
 			q->skb->dev = dev->dev;
 			q->skb->ip_summed = CHECKSUM_UNNECESSARY;
 			skb_record_rx_queue(q->skb, qid);
+			skb_mark_for_recycle(q->skb);
 
-			if (airoha_qdma_lro_rx_process(q, desc) < 0)
-				goto free_frag;
+			if (airoha_qdma_lro_rx_process(q, desc) < 0) {
+				dev_kfree_skb(q->skb);
+				q->skb = NULL;
+				continue;
+			}
 
 			q->skb->protocol = eth_type_trans(q->skb, dev->dev);
-			skb_mark_for_recycle(q->skb);
 		} else { /* scattered frame */
 			struct skb_shared_info *shinfo = skb_shinfo(q->skb);
 			int nr_frags = shinfo->nr_frags;
